==================================================
        TERRAFORM INSTALLATION ON LINUX
==================================================

This guide explains how to install Terraform on
a Linux (Ubuntu/Debian) machine.

--------------------------------------------------
STEP 1: Update Package Repository
--------------------------------------------------

Run:

sudo apt-get update


--------------------------------------------------
STEP 2: Fix dpkg Error (If Required)
--------------------------------------------------

If you get a dpkg configuration error while
installing packages, run:

sudo dpkg --configure -a

After that, update the package repository again:

sudo apt-get update


--------------------------------------------------
STEP 3: Install Required Packages
--------------------------------------------------

Install software-properties-common and curl:

sudo apt-get install -y software-properties-common curl


--------------------------------------------------
STEP 4: Add HashiCorp GPG Key
--------------------------------------------------

Add HashiCorp's GPG signing key:

curl -fsSL https://apt.releases.hashicorp.com/gpg | \
sudo tee /etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d/hashicorp.asc


--------------------------------------------------
STEP 5: Add HashiCorp Repository
--------------------------------------------------

Add the official HashiCorp APT repository:

sudo apt-add-repository "deb [arch=amd64] https://apt.releases.hashicorp.com $(lsb_release -cs) main"


--------------------------------------------------
STEP 6: Update Package Repository
--------------------------------------------------

Update the package list after adding the HashiCorp
repository:

sudo apt-get update


--------------------------------------------------
STEP 7: Install Terraform
--------------------------------------------------

Install Terraform:

sudo apt-get install -y terraform


--------------------------------------------------
STEP 8: Verify Terraform Installation
--------------------------------------------------

Check the installed Terraform version:

terraform -version

Example output:

Terraform v1.x.x
on linux_amd64


==================================================
                INSTALLATION COMPLETE
==================================================
